# Week 4 — Rule-Based Chatbot for the Campus Library

Name:UWINEZA Sharon
GitHub:Sharon-now

## Overview

This chatbot is a rule-based chatbot for the campus library. It helps students get information about library rooms, opening hours, borrowing and renewing books, fines, and printing services.

## Intents

| Tag      | Request                          | Example phrasing                   |
| -------- | -------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| rooms    | Find or book a library room      | “Can I book a study room?”         |
| hours    | Ask about library opening hours  | “What time does the library open?” |
| borrow   | Ask how to borrow a book         | “How can I borrow a book?”         |
| renew    | Ask how to renew a borrowed book | “Can I renew my book?”             |
| fines    | Ask about library fines          | “Do I have a fine?”                |
| printing | Ask about printing services      | “Can I print in the library?”      |

## Rule ordering

The rooms and borrow intents can collide because both may contain the word “book.” Rooms is checked before borrow because a user saying “I want to book a room” should be classified as rooms, not borrow. If the order were reversed, a room-booking request containing the word “book” could incorrectly be classified as borrow.

## The booking flow

The three values collected, in order, are:

1. Date
2. Time
3. Room

If an answer is not recognised, the chatbot asks the user to provide a valid answer before continuing with the booking.

## Test results

Test messages:35
Returned the expected tag: 35

## Running this notebook

Open `Sharon_UWINEZA_Assignment_4.ipynb` in Google Colab.

Run the cells in order. Do not use Run all because the chat cell waits for user input.

## What was learned

I learned how to build a rule-based chatbot using intents and keyword matching. I also learned that the order of rules is important because some messages can match more than one intent.
